{
 "id": "085-sari-ile-mavi-bulusunca",
 "lang": "en",
 "title": "When Yellow Meets Blue",
 "theme": "Mixing colours and painting together",
 "blurb": "Painting a picture for Teachers' Day, Can has only yellow paint and Elif has only blue. The meadow needs green! What will happen when yellow meets blue?",
 "voiceNames": {
  "can": "Can",
  "elif": "Elif",
  "nur": "Miss Nur"
 },
 "pages": [
  {
   "text": "Tomorrow is Teachers' Day. Can and Elif whispered together. “Let's paint a picture for Miss Nur!” said Can. “A great big, colourful picture!” said Elif. They put a great big sheet of paper on the easel. Brushes ready. Here we go!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Let's paint a picture for Miss Nur!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "A great big, colourful picture!"
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Can!",
   "ask": "If you made a present for your teacher, what would you make?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Can's pot had only yellow paint. Elif's pot had only blue. Can painted the sun, Elif painted the sky. “The meadow should be green,” said Can. Elif looked in her pot: “But there's no green!” Can felt fed up, and so did Elif. “Ohhh!”",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "The meadow should be green."
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "But there's no green! Ohhh!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Can has yellow, Elif has blue!",
    "msg": "You found the colours!"
   },
   "hint": "Which colour is Can's?",
   "ask": "Why were Can and Elif upset? What do you do when you feel fed up?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Elif took a deep breath: hhhhh… She let it out slowly: fwooo. Then her eyes lit up. “Can, I have an idea! What happens if yellow meets blue?” Can's eyebrows went up. “Let's try it!”",
   "hits": {
    "elif": {
     "say": "I have an idea!"
    },
    "can": {
     "say": "Let's try it!"
    }
   },
   "predict": {
    "q": "What do you think happens when yellow meets blue?",
    "res": "Let's see!",
    "opts": [
     {
      "l": "It turns green"
     },
     {
      "l": "It turns purple"
     }
    ]
   },
   "hint": "Touch Elif!",
   "ask": "Which colour do you think it will be? Why do you think so?"
  },
  {
   "text": "First the yellow paint: drip! Then the blue paint: drip! Now mix: swirl, swirl, swirl! Oh! Yellow met blue. It turned bright green! Can and Elif looked at each other: “Hooray!”",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "First yellow, then blue!"
    },
    "karistir": {
     "say": "Now mix: swirl, swirl, swirl!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Swirl, swirl, swirl! It's bright green!",
    "msg": "You mixed them!"
   },
   "hint": "Touch the yellow first!",
   "ask": "Have you ever mixed two colours? What colour did you get?"
  },
  {
   "text": "Can painted a blade of grass, then Elif. Swish swish, one by one! One, two, three, four, five. The meadow turned bright green. Can laughed, Elif laughed. The picture is done!",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "Your turn, Elif!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "One blade of grass from me!"
    }
   },
   "mech": {
    "done": "Five blades of grass! The meadow is bright green.",
    "msg": "Five blades of grass!"
   },
   "hint": "Count the grass!",
   "ask": "How did Can and Elif finish the picture together? What do you like doing with your friend?"
  },
  {
   "text": "On Teachers' Day morning, Can and Elif showed the picture to Miss Nur. “We're so lucky to have you!” they said. Miss Nur looked at the picture for a long time. “What a beautiful meadow! How did you find this green?” They both laughed at once: “Together!”",
   "hits": {
    "can": {
     "say": "We're so lucky to have you!"
    },
    "elif": {
     "say": "We made it together!"
    },
    "nur": {
     "say": "What a beautiful meadow! Thank you."
    }
   },
   "hint": "Touch Miss Nur!",
   "ask": "Would you like to tell your teacher “We're so lucky to have you”? How would you say it?"
  }
 ],
 "guide": {
  "kazanim": [
   "SNAB4 Artistic Practice (field skill): Decides on the art activity to do (painting a picture for the teacher), uses the materials at hand and makes a new colour by mixing two colours.",
   "SNAB.2 Examining a work of art: Examines Can and Elif's picture, asks questions about the picture and expresses feelings and thoughts about the work (SNAB.2.g).",
   "TAOB.2 Making meaning from visual materials: Predicts what will happen by looking at the paint blobs on the page; connects colour mixing to their own daily life (TAOB.2.a).",
   "SDB2.2 Cooperation and D4 Friendship: Solves a problem that can't be solved alone by combining materials with a friend; paints in turns and gives the shared work as a present together."
  ],
  "once": [
   "Show the cover: 'What do you think happens when yellow meets blue?' Listen to the guesses without correcting, then say 'Let's see in the story.'",
   "Find yellow and blue objects in the classroom together.",
   "Ask 'What is Teachers' Day? How can we thank our teacher?'"
  ],
  "sirasi": [
   "On page 1, say that Teachers' Day is celebrated on 24 November.",
   "On page 2, let the child touch Can first, then his colour; do the same for Elif. Ask 'Why should the meadow be green?'",
   "On page 3, breathe together with Elif: 'hhhhh… fwooo'. Welcome both answers to the prediction question with curiosity.",
   "On page 4, say the order out loud: 'First yellow, then blue, then mix'; touch Elif to mix.",
   "On page 5, count the blades of grass together: 'One, two, three, four, five!' Point out that Can and Elif painted in turns.",
   "On page 6, say the word “Together!” with the child, all in one voice."
  ],
  "sonra": [
   "Why were Can and Elif fed up? What did Elif do to find an idea?",
   "How did the green paint appear? Was your guess right?",
   "How do the yellow sun, the blue sky and the green meadow in the picture make you feel?",
   "Look closely at the picture: Which colour do you see where? Which part did you like most, and why?"
  ],
  "sinif": {
   "ad": "Colours meet: a shared meadow picture",
   "sure": "20 min",
   "materyal": "Yellow and blue finger paint (or gouache), small pots, large kraft paper, brushes, aprons, a damp cloth",
   "adim": [
    "Pair the children up; give one only yellow paint and the other only blue.",
    "Ask for predictions first: 'What happens if we mix the two colours?' Note the guesses on the board as pictures (coloured dots).",
    "Each pair puts one drop of yellow and one drop of blue and mixes them; they name the colour they get and compare it with their guess.",
    "All the pairs paint green blades of grass on the big paper in turns; look at the shared meadow picture together and hang it on the board as a thank-you picture for the teacher or the school staff."
   ]
  },
  "evSoru": [
   "Which colour did Can have, and which colour did Elif have?",
   "What happened when yellow met blue?",
   "What would you like to do together with a friend?"
  ],
  "evEtk": {
   "ad": "Colours meeting in the kitchen",
   "d": "Put water in two clear glasses; drop yellow food colouring (or watercolour) in one and blue in the other. Ask your child 'What happens when they mix?' and listen to the guess. Then mix the two colours together in a third glass and talk about the colour you get. If you like, try red and yellow, and red and blue too."
  },
  "aileNotu": "Today we read 'When Yellow Meets Blue'. While painting a picture for Teachers' Day, Can and Elif noticed they only had yellow and blue paint; with Elif's idea they mixed the colours, found green and finished the picture together. The story supports colour mixing, making predictions and cooperation. Mixing two colours together at home and asking 'What do you think will happen?' will grow this curiosity."
 },
